se transactions' or 'staking in gambling' takes the 6th-Case-affix.\n\nTerms: विभक्ति-6", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["व्यवहृपणोः समर्थयोः २.३.५७", "२.३.५७", "२.३.५७ व्यवहृपणोः समर्थयोः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vyavahfpaRoH samarTayoH २.३.५७", "२.३.५७", "२.३.५७ vyavahfpaRoH samarTayoH"]}], "vyatyayo bahulam": [{"id": "vyatyayo bahulam", "headword": "व्यत्ययो बहुलम्", "headword_slp1": "vyatyayo bahulam", "fold": "vyatyayo bahulam", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In the छन्दस् (Vedas) there is diversely an interchange of the various विकरण-as शप् etc. which have been previously ordained under special circumstances.\n\nTerms: छन्दस्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["व्यत्ययो बहुलम् ३.१.८५", "३.१.८५", "३.१.८५ व्यत्ययो बहुलम्"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vyatyayo bahulam ३.१.८५", "३.१.८५", "३.१.८५ vyatyayo bahulam"]}], "vyaDajaporanupasarge": [{"id": "vyaDajaporanupasarge", "headword": "व्यधजपोरनुपसर्गे", "headword_slp1": "vyaDajaporanupasarge", "fold": "vyaDajaporanupasarge", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix अप् comes after the verbs 1. व्यध् 'to hurt or to pierce' 2. जप् 'to mutter' when no उपसर्ग is in composition with them.\n\nTerms: अप्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["व्यधजपोरनुपसर्गे ३.३.६१", "३.३.६१", "३.३.६१ व्यधजपोरनुपसर्गे"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vyaDajaporanupasarge ३.३.६१", "३.३.६१", "३.३.६१ vyaDajaporanupasarge"]}], "vyan sapatne": [{"id": "vyan sapatne", "headword": "व्यन् सपत्ने", "headword_slp1": "vyan sapatne", "fold": "vyan sapatne", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix व्यत् comes after the word भ्रातृ when the sense is that of 'an enemy'.\n\nTerms: व्यत्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["व्यन् सपत्ने ४.१.१४५", "४.१.१४५", "४.१.१४५ व्यन् सपत्ने"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vyan sapatne ४.१.१४५", "४.१.१४५", "४.१.१४५ vyan sapatne"]}], "vyaharati mfgaH": [{"id": "vyAharati mfgaH", "headword": "व्याहरति मृगः", "headword_slp1": "vyAharati mfgaH", "fold": "vyaharati mfgaH", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "An affix comes after a word in the Locative -7th case in construction denoting time, in the sense of 'who then wanders' and the word so formed refers to a wild beast.\n\nTerms: विभक्ति-7", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["व्याहरति मृगः ४.३.५१", "४.३.५१", "४.३.५१ व्याहरति मृगः"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vyAharati mfgaH ४.३.५१", "४.३.५१", "४.३.५१ vyAharati mfgaH"]}], "vyaYjanErupasikte": [{"id": "vyaYjanErupasikte", "headword": "व्यञ्जनैरुपसिक्ते", "headword_slp1": "vyaYjanErupasikte", "fold": "vyaYjanErupasikte", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The affix ठक् comes after a word denoting a condiment, being in the Instrumental -3rd case in construction when the sense is 'sprinkled therewith'.\n\nTerms: ठक्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["व्यञ्जनैरुपसिक्ते ४.४.२६", "४.४.२६", "४.४.२६ व्यञ्जनैरुपसिक्ते"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vyaYjanErupasikte ४.४.२६", "४.४.२६", "४.४.२६ vyaYjanErupasikte"]}], "vyasca": [{"id": "vyaSca", "headword": "व्यश्च", "headword_slp1": "vyaSca", "fold": "vyasca", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "The semi-vowel of व्या (व्ये) 'to cover' is not vocalised when the affix ल्यप् follows.\n\nTerms: सम्प्रसारणम्", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["व्यश्च ६.१.४३", "६.१.४३", "६.१.४३ व्यश्च"], "synonyms_slp1": ["vyaSca ६.१.४३", "६.१.४३", "६.१.४३ vyaSca"]}], "vyavayinontaram": [{"id": "vyavAyino'ntaram", "headword": "व्यवायिनोऽन्तरम्", "headword_slp1": "vyavAyino'ntaram", "fold": "vyavayinontaram", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "ashtadhyayi-english", "senses": [{"gloss": "In a बहुव्रीहि समास ending in अन्तर the acute accent (उदात्त) is on the final after a word which denotes 'that which lies between'.\n\nTerms: समास end acute-2nd-term", "gloss_language": "en"}], "syno